COPY strapi.partners (id, document_id, name, affiliation, role, description, show_name_on_logo, created_at, updated_at, published_at, created_by_id, updated_by_id, locale) FROM stdin;
218	o48lmnf066t1fg958b4z2pl8	GrowGraph	\N	\N	Growgraph contributes to the development of the AI Library’s LLM Philosopher Personas module. As a company specializing in large-scale knowledge graph engineering and AI-driven data structuring, Growgraph brings technical expertise in semantic architectures, concept-mapping and model alignment. Its involvement strengthens the module’s ability to ground philosophical personas in structured knowledge networks, ensuring more robust reasoning, contextual accuracy and nuanced engagement with classical texts.	t	2025-11-13 13:12:07.345	2025-11-21 13:56:37.636	2025-11-21 13:59:22.29	\N	\N	en
216	pvvw37kmgpk5ujo8khlnder9	Amidex	Aix-Marseille University	\N	A*Midex (Aix-Marseille Initiative of Excellence) funded the first major wave of digitisation for the AI Library between 2019 and 2022, enabling the creation of high-quality digital corpora of philosophical and scientific texts. It also supported the early prototyping of the AI Library’s LLM-based Philosopher Personas, providing the resources needed to explore how large language models can emulate reasoning styles and conceptual frameworks drawn from major thinkers. This dual support established the foundational infrastructure for the current AI Library module.	f	2025-11-13 13:10:26.216	2025-11-21 13:58:06.553	2025-11-21 13:58:06.576	\N	\N	en
217	ozjyg0wxb5okt30qp67f7fi5	CGGG	Aix-Marseille University	\N	The Centre Gilles Gaston Granger (CGGG) at Aix-Marseille University, a joint CNRS–AMU research laboratory specializing in epistemology, history of philosophy and philosophy of science, hosted the development of the AI Library Module. Its expertise in the analysis of scientific knowledge and digital tools provided the conceptual foundations for the LLM philosopher module.	f	2025-10-05 08:23:20.411	2025-11-21 13:58:16.421	2025-11-21 13:58:16.446	\N	\N	en
199	ea40fagdo36qi6qwf75bguzu	 LIS	Aix-Marseille University	\N	The LIS is a computer science laboratory at Aix-Marseille University and one of France’s major research units in algorithms, data science and digital systems. It hosted part of the development of the AI Library module, providing expertise in software engineering, data processing and computational infrastructures. This contribution helped shape the module’s technical foundations and ensured its integration within robust and scalable digital architectures.	f	2025-09-29 16:10:42.952	2025-11-25 06:12:22.946	\N	\N	\N	en
200	ea40fagdo36qi6qwf75bguzu	 LIS	Aix-Marseille University	\N	The LIS is a computer science laboratory at Aix-Marseille University and one of France’s major research units in algorithms, data science and digital systems. It hosted part of the development of the AI Library module, providing expertise in software engineering, data processing and computational infrastructures. This contribution helped shape the module’s technical foundations and ensured its integration within robust and scalable digital architectures.	f	2025-09-29 16:10:42.952	2025-11-25 06:12:22.946	2025-11-25 06:12:22.982	\N	\N	en
201	zkz4oiikl284rlr0amciqtk7	IRASIA	\N	\N	IRASIA is contribution to Knowledge Tree by its own database of mentorship in China Studies.	f	2025-11-25 06:32:59.077	2025-11-25 15:25:33.113	\N	\N	\N	en
202	ozjyg0wxb5okt30qp67f7fi5	CGGG	Aix-Marseille University	\N	The Centre Gilles Gaston Granger (CGGG) at Aix-Marseille University, a joint CNRS–AMU research laboratory specializing in epistemology, history of philosophy and philosophy of science, hosted the development of the AI Library Module. Its expertise in the analysis of scientific knowledge and digital tools provided the conceptual foundations for the LLM philosopher module.	f	2025-10-05 08:23:20.411	2025-11-21 13:58:16.421	\N	\N	\N	en
203	gkuj5voxbtc5pdkywxpcej3x	Insciam	Aix-Marseille University	\N	Insciam has financed the prototype of the LLM-based Philosopher Personas within the AI Library module. As an organisation focused on advancing research at the intersection of knowledge, technology and intellectual history, Insciam supports projects that rethink how scholarly tools are built and used. Its contribution has enabled the development of a first working version of the philosopher personas, allowing the module to model reasoning styles, argumentative structures and conceptual frameworks inspired by major thinkers, and to integrate them into a broader AI-assisted environment for exploring classic texts and ideas.	t	2025-11-13 13:14:39.144	2025-11-21 13:56:22.947	\N	\N	\N	en
204	pvd86ub41eonyg49grbpbc8t	France 2030	\N	\N	France 2030 supported the development of the prototype for the AI Library module, with a specific focus on the LLM Philosopher Persona component. France 2030 is a national investment plan launched by the French government to accelerate strategic innovations in science, technology and culture, funding projects that bridge advanced research with transformative digital tools. Through this support, the LLM Philosopher Persona module benefited from a framework designed to promote cutting-edge AI development and to foster new forms of interaction between humanities research and artificial intelligence.	f	2025-11-13 13:20:29.726	2025-11-21 13:59:41.175	\N	\N	\N	en
205	o48lmnf066t1fg958b4z2pl8	GrowGraph	\N	\N	Growgraph contributes to the development of the AI Library’s LLM Philosopher Personas module. As a company specializing in large-scale knowledge graph engineering and AI-driven data structuring, Growgraph brings technical expertise in semantic architectures, concept-mapping and model alignment. Its involvement strengthens the module’s ability to ground philosophical personas in structured knowledge networks, ensuring more robust reasoning, contextual accuracy and nuanced engagement with classical texts.	t	2025-11-13 13:12:07.345	2025-11-21 13:56:37.636	\N	\N	\N	en
206	p9vudcq157ve9jjeicvqilt9	Centre Bentham	Sciences Po Paris	\N	The Bentham Center in Paris is partnering with LEGACY to find funding for the automated transcription of Jeremy Bentham French Manuscripts. 	f	2025-11-25 06:17:10.889	2025-11-25 06:19:13.208	\N	\N	\N	en
207	c24qncdkxplcbx295k1xgok5	Inria Almanach Team	\N	\N	The Inria Almanach team provides expert guidance on the digitisation of manuscripts for the AI Library. As a research group specializing in natural language processing, digital texts, and large-scale corpus analysis, Almanach brings advanced expertise in OCR, text normalisation, and the preparation of historical documents for computational use. Their support strengthens the AI Library’s capacity to process complex manuscripts and to integrate high-quality digital editions into its knowledge systems.	t	2025-11-13 14:10:02.975	2025-11-25 06:29:02.033	\N	\N	\N	en
